<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $189.9 mln Feb 7.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $189.9 mln Feb 7.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $189.9 million surplus on Feb 7 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 7</p>
<p>Exports: $229.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $175 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $289.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $153.8 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $189.9 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $993 million</p>
<p>Imports: $797 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.121 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $922 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $395 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
